(The Uncertainty Principle, formulated by Werner Heisenberg in 1927, states) Tj
72 9786 Td
(that there is a fundamental limit to the precision with which certain pairs) Tj
72 9772 Td
(of physical properties can be simultaneously known.

In other words, the) Tj
72 9758 Td
(more precisely you measure a particle's position, the less precisely you) Tj
72 9744 Td
(can know its momentum, and vice versa. This is not a limitation of our) Tj
72 9730 Td
(measuring instruments—it is a fundamental property of the) Tj
72 9716 Td
(universe.

Quantum mechanics replaced classical physics at the microscopic) Tj
72 9702 Td
(level. Particles behave as both waves and particles \(wave-particle) Tj
72 9688 Td
